<title>SWITZERLAND: ABB sets new Vietnam venture.</title>
<headline>ABB sets new Vietnam venture.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>ABB Asea Brown Boveri Ltd said it had formed a joint venture in Vietnam to produce advanced switchgear and transformers for the domestic market.</p>
<p>ABB owns 65 percent of  ABB Transformers and Switchgear Ltd, while state-owned THIBIDI has the rest. The new venture in Ho Chi Minh City employs 380 people and makes distribution transformers up to 10,000 kVA, mainly for use in power distribution networks.</p>
<p>ABB established its first joint venture in Hanoi in 1994 to manufacture power transmission and distribution products.</p>
<p>-- Zurich newsroom +41 1 631 7340</p>
